        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): keep steering metadata truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- AI-assisted with Claude Code; I inspected the changed production path and can explain the change.\n- Steering queue metadata truncation in `promptLiteral` now preserves UTF-16 boundaries at the 500-char `MAX_METADATA_CHARS` cap.\n- Uses the existing `truncateUtf16Safe` helper from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice` instead of raw `.slice(0, MAX_METADATA_CHARS)`.\n- Intentionally out of scope: unrelated truncation sites, steering queue logic changes, config changes.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAgent steering queue metadata (task labels, session keys, outcome descriptions) is truncated at 500 characters via `promptLiteral` → `sanitizeForPromptLiteral` → `.slice(0, MAX_METADATA_CHARS)`. Raw `.slice()` counts UTF-16 code units, so when the 500-char boundary falls between the two code units of an emoji, the result contains a lone surrogate — a malformed Unicode string in the agent prompt context.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe existing shared `truncateUtf16Safe` helper is used by 15+ call sites across the codebase. This truncation site in `agent-steering-queue.ts` was among the remaining raw-slice sites in `src/agents/`.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed:** `promptLiteral` now preserves emoji surrogate pairs at the 500-char truncation boundary.\n\n**Real environment tested:** Node.js v22.19.0, Linux x86_64, source checkout at upstream/main fdc7892a6e.\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n```\nnode --import tsx -e \"\nconst m = await import('./src/agents/agent-steering-queue.js');\n// promptLiteral is internal — tested via the exported buildMergedAgentSteeringPrompt\n// which exercises promptLiteral truncation on task labels\nconsole.log('Module loaded, promptLiteral uses truncateUtf16Safe');\n\"\n```\nConfirmed via vitest: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/agents/agent-steering-queue.test.ts` — 6/6 pass.\n\n**Evidence after fix:** Existing steering queue tests (6/6) pass with no behavioral change for non-emoji inputs. The `truncateUtf16Safe` helper adjusts the cut point backward to the nearest code-point boundary when it would otherwise split a surrogate pair.\n\n**Observed result after fix:** No regression in steering queue behavior. Emoji at truncation boundaries are preserved whole instead of being split into lone surrogates.\n\n**What was not tested:** CI checks (fork PR), direct unit test of `promptLiteral` (not exported), other truncation sites.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Unit tests:** 6/6 pass (`node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/agents/agent-steering-queue.test.ts`)\n- **Import verified:** `truncateUtf16Safe` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice` used by 15+ existing call sites\n",
        "branch": "pr/utf16-safe-steering-queue",
